  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA containing NNN integers.\n\nConsider the following process:\n\n\nLet S=0S = 0S=0 initially.\nFor each iii from 111 to NNN **in order**, update SSS to either (S+Ai)(S+A_i)(S+Ai​) or (S×Ai)(S\\times A_i)(S×Ai​).\n\nThat is, either add AiA_iAi​ to SSS or multiply SSS by AiA_iAi​.\nBefore performing the process, you're allowed to freely rearrange the elements of AAA as you like.\n\nIf you choose the rearrangement of AAA and the sequence of operations optimally, what's the **maximum** possible value of SSS that you can obtain?\n\nThis maximum value can be very large, so print it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of elements in the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ - the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible value of SSS, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n4 2 5 2\n3\n1 2 1",
        "output": "80\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Choose the rearrangement A=[2,2,5,4]A = [2, 2, 5, 4]A=[2,2,5,4]. Then,\n\nAdd A1=2A_1 = 2A1​=2 to SSS. Now, S=2S = 2S=2.\nAdd A2=2A_2 = 2A2​=2 to SSS. Now, S=4S = 4S=4.\nMultiply SSS by A3=5A_3 = 5A3​=5. Now, S=20S = 20S=20.\nMultiply SSS by A4=4A_4 = 4A4​=4. Now, S=80S = 80S=80.\n\nThis is the maximum value that can be obtained.\nTest case 222: Choose any rearrangement and sum up all the numbers to get 1+1+2=41+1+2 = 41+1+2=4.\nThis is the maximum value that can be obtained."
      }
    ]
  },
